  "verbalization": "Licochalcone D appears to have a shared target of SNU-387 in all three provided paths, suggesting a potential mechanism of action involving this cell line. SNU-387 is identified as a target of both S-ethylcysteine zwitterion and Dendocarbin K, with the latter also targeting CD276 antigen. This indicates that Licochalcone D may act through a common pathway, possibly by modulating the activity of SNU-387, which in turn influences CD276 antigen expression. The presence of multiple targets and their shared relationship with CD276 antigen suggests a possible regulatory or inhibitory role for Licochalcone D in the context of SNU-387, potentially through a mechanism involving receptor activation or signaling pathways. The evidence supports a link between Licochalcone D and CD276 antigen, but the exact nature of the interaction remains to be elucidated.",
